# =============================================================================
# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next Q8_0 at 262144 -- the quality reference, full context
# =============================================================================
# See qwen38-flash-next-q8-128k.env for why Q8_0 leaves ~94 GiB on the host, and
# qwen38-flash-next-q4km-128k.env for the architecture and the placement sweep.
#
# The context itself is cheap here for the same reason it is cheap on the Q4
# side -- the hybrid keeps a KV cache on only every 4th layer, so 262144 costs
# 4337 MiB of cache instead of the ~24 GiB a dense model of this shape would
# want. What is NOT cheap is the compute buffer, which scales with -ub times
# n_kv. Unlike the Q4 256k profile, -ub stays at 2048 here: -ncmoe 20 has already
# surrendered enough VRAM to pay for it, and on Q8 the micro-batch is worth far
# more than the expert layer a smaller one would buy (see the 128k profile).
#
# --- MEASURED 2026-09-03, sweep-bench, -c 262144, -ncmoe 20, -ub 2048 --------
#
#   CUDA0 weights  75 970    host 103 524    KV 4 337    compute 12 628
#   2162.7 pp / 36.9 tg at N_KV 0-2048
#
# Against the 128k profile (2302.7 pp / 40.6 tg): the doubled context costs
# 6.1 % prefill and 9.1 % generation, paid as three more expert layers pushed to
# the host. That is a real cost, unlike on the Q4 side where 256k was nearly
# free -- because Q8_0 is already ~10 GiB past what the card can hold, every
# byte the context takes comes straight out of resident weights.
#
# HOST RAM IS THE RISK ON THIS ONE. ~101 GiB of resident weights, plus page cache
# for a 176 GB file, plus whatever a deep prefill transiently allocates. RESULTS
# 26.3 records llama-server reaching 203 GiB RSS on a 250k prefill (a smaller
# model) and being OOM-killed. Watch `free -g` the first time this profile sees
# a genuinely deep prompt, and drop to the 128k variant if it bites.
#
#   ./serve.sh qwen38-flash-next-q8-256k
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

: "${IK_MODEL_GLOB:=${IK_MODELS_ROOT}/lmstudio-community/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Q8_0-00001-of-*.gguf}"

: "${IK_ALIAS:=qwen38-flash-next-q8-256k}"
: "${IK_CTX:=262144}"

: "${IK_RTR:=0}"

# 20, not the 17 of the 128k profile: the extra 2.1 GiB of KV plus the compute
# buffer growing 6996 -> 12 628 has to come out of resident weights.
: "${IK_FIT:=0}"
: "${IK_NCMOE:=20}"

# 2048 stays, unlike the Q4 256k profile. There, -ub 2048 simply would not fit;
# here it does, because -ncmoe 20 has already surrendered the VRAM. And it is
# worth keeping: on the Q8 file the micro-batch drives prefill roughly 2:1 while
# an expert layer is worth ~3 % of generation.
: "${IK_UBATCH:=2048}"
: "${IK_BATCH:=2048}"

: "${IK_CTK:=q8_0}"
: "${IK_CTV:=q8_0}"

: "${IK_THREADS:=8}"
: "${IK_THREADS_BATCH:=24}"
